-- Regression fixture for issue #920.
--
-- `Verdict` is declared twice, so naming it in a GIVETH is genuinely ambiguous.
-- The ONE error the user should see is that ambiguity.
--
-- What used to happen instead: resolution handed back an `OutOfScope` sentinel
-- with an unregistered unique, and checking the body against that poisoned
-- signature produced, per branch of the IF, both
--
--   "I've encountered a resolved name that has no additional information
--    stored for it: Verdict. This is an error in this system and should be
--    reported as a bug."
--
-- and the vacuous
--
--   "must match its type signature ... namely Verdict but is here of type
--    Verdict"
--
-- -- five diagnostics for one mistake, four of them noise, and one of them
-- accusing the compiler of a bug the user had not hit.
--
-- The golden for this file must therefore contain exactly the ambiguity error.

DECLARE Verdict IS ONE OF yes, no

DECLARE Verdict IS ONE OF maybe, perhaps

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Verdict
`decide it` MEANS IF x THEN yes ELSE no
